  "description": "Northwest Orient's scheme of the 1970s and 80s: a white crown, a navy band through the windows from the forward door aft, bare metal below it, and a plain red fin. 'NORTHWEST ORIENT' in red capitals over the forward windows with the red and white NW roundel after it. Bare metal engines. Worn by its 727s, DC-10s, 747s and, from 1985, 757s ('Orient' dropped from the titles in 1986).",
